'''Line E''' of the [[CristoCarril]] (CC) system is a commuter rail line operated by [[Intercon]] that runs on the [[Sant Bart Line]] corridor between the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[La Llacuna (CristoCarril)|La Llacuna]] in [[Els Aiguamolls (comarca)|Els Aiguamolls]]. The line covers 42.4 km and serves 17 stations across two comarcas — [[Sant Cristòfor (comarca)|Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Els Aiguamolls (comarca)|Els Aiguamolls]]. It is the fifth CristoCarril line, complementing [[Line A (CristoCarril)|Line A]] on the [[Coastal Line]] corridor, [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]] on the [[Portnou Line]] corridor, [[Line C (CristoCarril)|Line C]] on the [[Varakí Line]] corridor, and [[Line D (CristoCarril)|Line D]] on the [[Via Sud Line]] corridor.

Line E follows a northern route from the Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal, through the ciutats of Sant Cristòfor — [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], [[Sant Miquel (ciutat)|Sant Miquel]], and [[Costa Nord (ciutat)|Costa Nord]] — before entering the [[Els Aiguamolls (comarca)|Els Aiguamolls comarca]] and serving the settlements of Aiguamolls Sud, Els Canyars, and La Llacuna. The line shares the first five stations with [[Line D (CristoCarril)|Line D]] on the Sant Bart Line corridor before Line D diverges onto the Old Grand Subdivision at Mas Blanc, while Line E continues north along the Sant Bart Line. The terminus at [[La Llacuna (CristoCarril)|La Llacuna]] provides a shuttle connection to [[L'Estany Airport]].

== Route ==

=== Sant Cristòfor ===

Line E begins at the [[Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal]] in [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], the city's primary rail hub, shared with [[Line B (CristoCarril)|Line B]], [[Line C (CristoCarril)|Line C]], and [[Line D (CristoCarril)|Line D]]. From the terminal, the line heads south through three stations in Original — [[Portal de Sant Cristòfor Station|Portal de Sant Cristòfor]], [[Sant Pere (CristoCarril)|Sant Pere]], and [[La Font (CristoCarril)|La Font]] — serving the dense residential neighbourhoods south of the historic core. These four stations are shared with Lines B, C, and D. At La Font, Line B diverges to follow the [[Portnou Line]] corridor through [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]] and [[Sant Llorenç (ciutat)|Sant Llorenç]], while Line C continues on the [[Varakí Line]] corridor through the eastern ciutats. Lines D and E continue together on the Sant Bart Line corridor for one additional station.

The line then serves two stations in [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]]: [[Mas Blanc (CristoCarril)|Mas Blanc]], shared with Line D, and [[Parc de Sant Jordi (CristoCarril)|Parc de Sant Jordi]]. At Mas Blanc, Line D diverges onto the Old Grand Subdivision, heading southeast through central Sant Jordi toward Ciutat del Pujol and Cumará. Line E continues north on the Sant Bart Line, curving through the eastern neighbourhoods of Sant Jordi before entering [[Sant Miquel (ciutat)|Sant Miquel]].

The line serves three stations in Sant Miquel: [[Sant Miquel Sud (CristoCarril)|Sant Miquel Sud]], [[Sant Miquel Centre (CristoCarril)|Sant Miquel Centre]], and [[Sant Miquel Nord (CristoCarril)|Sant Miquel Nord]]. Sant Miquel is a residential ciutat in the northern part of Sant Cristòfor, and these stations provide the primary commuter rail connection for the area.

Continuing north, the line enters [[Costa Nord (ciutat)|Costa Nord]], serving five stations: [[Les Dunes (CristoCarril)|Les Dunes]], [[Costa Centre (CristoCarril)|Costa Centre]], [[El Far (CristoCarril)|El Far]], [[Platja Llevant (CristoCarril)|Platja Llevant]], and [[Costa Nord (CristoCarril)|Costa Nord]]. Costa Nord is a coastal ciutat on the northern edge of Sant Cristòfor, and these stations serve the coastal neighbourhoods and the ciutat's residential districts. The 14 stations within Sant Cristòfor cover the central and northern districts of the city.

=== Els Aiguamolls ===

After leaving Sant Cristòfor, Line E enters the [[Els Aiguamolls (comarca)|Els Aiguamolls comarca]] and serves three stations: [[Aiguamolls Sud (CristoCarril)|Aiguamolls Sud]], [[Els Canyars (CristoCarril)|Els Canyars]], and [[La Llacuna (CristoCarril)|La Llacuna]]. Els Aiguamolls is a wetland comarca in northern Estret Province, and the line provides the primary commuter rail connection between the comarca's settlements and Sant Cristòfor. [[La Llacuna (CristoCarril)|La Llacuna]] station is the northernmost terminus of the CristoCarril system and serves as the principal rail hub for the southern Els Aiguamolls communities. The station also provides a shuttle connection to [[L'Estany Airport]], the nearest airport to the Els Aiguamolls comarca.

