== Service pattern ==

Line E operates three service patterns between [[Sant Cristòfor]] and [[La Llacuna (CristoCarril)|La Llacuna]]:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Stops !! Stations served !! Travel time
|-
| '''Short''' || All stops 1–14 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to Costa Nord || ~37 min
|-
| '''Express''' || 1, 2, 5, 8, 11, 14, 17 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to La Llacuna, skipping intermediate stations || ~45 min
|-
| '''Local''' || All stops 1–17 || Sant Cristòfor Central Terminal to La Llacuna || ~55 min
|}

The '''short''' service operates entirely within [[Sant Cristòfor]], running from the Central Terminal through the central and northern ciutats — [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Jordi (ciutat)|Sant Jordi]], [[Sant Miquel (ciutat)|Sant Miquel]], and [[Costa Nord (ciutat)|Costa Nord]] — to Costa Nord station on the northern edge of the city. This is the most frequent service, providing high-capacity commuter rail for the residential districts of northern Sant Cristòfor.

The '''express''' service provides the fastest connection between Sant Cristòfor and La Llacuna, stopping at the Central Terminal, Portal de Sant Cristòfor, Mas Blanc, Sant Miquel Centre, Costa Centre, Costa Nord, and La Llacuna. The express skips most suburban stations within Sant Cristòfor and all intermediate stations in Els Aiguamolls, reducing the end-to-end journey to approximately 45 minutes. The express is primarily used by long-distance commuters between Sant Cristòfor and the Els Aiguamolls communities.

The '''local''' service stops at all 17 stations along the full 42.4 km route, with an end-to-end journey time of approximately 55 minutes. The local provides the only CristoCarril service to the intermediate stations in Sant Jordi (Parc de Sant Jordi), Sant Miquel (Sant Miquel Sud, Sant Miquel Nord), Costa Nord (Les Dunes, El Far, Platja Llevant), and Els Aiguamolls (Aiguamolls Sud, Els Canyars).

== Schedule ==

Line E operates from approximately 5:00 AM to 12:30 AM daily. Frequencies vary by service pattern and time of day:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Service !! Peak (7–10 AM, 4–7 PM) !! Off-peak (daytime) !! Evening (after 8 PM) !! Weekend
|-
| '''Short''' || every 10 min || every 15 min || every 20 min || every 20 min (daytime), every 30 min (evening)
|-
| '''Express''' || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 90 min || every 60 min (daytime), every 90 min (evening)
|-
| '''Local''' || every 30 min || every 60 min || every 90 min || every 60 min (daytime), every 90 min (evening)
|}

The short service is the most frequent, reflecting the high commuter demand within central and northern Sant Cristòfor. The express provides a regular connection between Sant Cristòfor and La Llacuna, with reduced evening and weekend frequency. The local is the least frequent, reflecting the lower ridership at the intermediate stations in outer Sant Cristòfor and Els Aiguamolls. Combined, the three services provide up to 9 trains per hour at the Central Terminal during peak periods.

== Fares ==

Line E uses the [[Tarifa Integrada]] fare system, which is shared across the CristoCarril network and integrated with the [[Metro de Sant Cristòfor]] and [[Rodalies de Portnou]] systems. The line operates a flat fare of B$2.50 for all journeys, regardless of distance travelled.

Passengers using a [[Tarifa Integrada]] smart card receive free transfers to connecting metro, streetcar, and Rodalies services within a 90-minute window. Concession fares (half price) are available to seniors, students, and children under 12. Children under 5 travel free. Monthly and weekly passes are available with discounts of up to 40% off the single-ride fare.

